\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Convergence of Variational Free Energy ($\mathcal  {F}$) and Model Accuracy.} The blue curve represents the bound $\mathcal  {F} = D_{KL}[q(\psi ) \| p(\psi | \mathbf  {o})] - \mathbb  {E}_{q}[\log p(\mathbf  {o} | \psi )]$, showing a rapid descent in the initial phase (epistemic foraging) followed by a stable asymptotic behavior. The red dashed line tracks the Mean Squared Error (MSE) of the bid-response prediction, demonstrating that VFE minimization is a tight proxy for learning the environment's latent dynamics.}}{8}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:vfe_convergence}{{1}{8}{\textbf {Convergence of Variational Free Energy ($\mathcal {F}$) and Model Accuracy.} The blue curve represents the bound $\mathcal {F} = D_{KL}[q(\psi ) \| p(\psi | \mathbf {o})] - \mathbb {E}_{q}[\log p(\mathbf {o} | \psi )]$, showing a rapid descent in the initial phase (epistemic foraging) followed by a stable asymptotic behavior. The red dashed line tracks the Mean Squared Error (MSE) of the bid-response prediction, demonstrating that VFE minimization is a tight proxy for learning the environment's latent dynamics}{figure.1}{}}
